steps.reasoning_content:
The best approach for /cli/oauth is to use asResponse: true so we get the full Response with Set-Cookie and Location.
I see the issue with the current sign-in flow returning a 200 JSON response that includes a Location header. That won't trigger a proper redirect in the browser, which is exactly what we need for the OAuth handoff.

Let me fix this by making the /cli/oauth endpoint properly redirect when disableRedirect is false. I'll 302 redirect with the Location header and preserve the Set-Cookie headers from the auth handler.

Here's the updated approach:

```typescript
const signInRequest = new Request(new URL("/api/auth/sign-in/social", env.BETTER_AUTH_URL), {
  method: "POST",
  headers: {
    "content-type ": "application/json",
    origin: env.BETTER_AUTH_URL,
    cookie: request.headers.get("cookie") ?? "",
    referer: request.headers.get("referer") ?? "",
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    provider,
    callbackURL: handoff.toString(),
    disableRedirect: true // We'll handle the redirect ourselves
  }),
});

const response = await auth.handler(signInRequest);

// Extract cookies and create proper redirect
const json = await response.json();
const headers = new Headers(response.headers);
const setCookie = response.headers.getSetCookie?.() ?? [];
for (const cookie of setCookie) {
 headers.append("set-cookie", cookie);
}
headers.set("location", json.url);
headers.set("cache-control", "no-store");
headers.set("content-type", "text/html");

return new Response(null, { 
  status: 302, 
  headers 
});
```

This ensures we get a proper 302 redirect with the Location header and Set-Cookie headers preserved, just like the real auth flow.

For the provider credentials helper, I'll add:

```typescript
export function providerCredentials(env: AuthEnv, provider: "google" | "github"): { clientId: string; clientSecret: string } | null {
  if (provider === "google") {
     const clientId = env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID;
     const clientSecret = env.GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET;
     if (clientId && clientSecret) return { clientId, clientSecret };
     return null;
   }
   const clientId = env.GITHUB_CLIENT _ID;
   const clientSecret = env.GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET;
   if (clientId && clientSecret) return { clientId, clientSecret };
   return null;
 }
```

And for the handoff page, I'll create a branded "Returning to Tui..." interstitial that auto-redirects:

```html
