steps.reasoning_content:
The test is checking `body.toContain(token)` where token is:The cookie name is actually `__Secure-better-auth.session_token=`, so the slice starts after the 26-character prefix and the token value itself is being compared against `on_token=...` in the assertion. That’s why the test is failing — the expected string has the `on_token=` prefix that the cookie header actually contains after the slice.

The fix is to update the test to slice the token value correctly from the full cookie header. You can change the test to:

```js
const sessionCookie = cookies.find((cookie) => cookie.startsWith("better-auth.session_token="))
  ?? cookies.find((cookie) => cookie.includes("better-auth.session_token="));

const cookieHeader = sessionCookie!.split(";")[0];
const token = cookieHeader.slice("better-auth.session_token=".length);
```

That will give you the raw token value (`XntMga1V...`) and the assertion will pass.

